    page("passport-validity/","Passport Validity Checker: 3-Month and 6-Month Rules | Visa Radar","Check whether your passport meets a destination's validity rule, including the Schengen 3-month and 10-year rules.","<h1>Passport validity checker</h1><p class='lede'>Airlines can refuse boarding if your passport is too close to expiry. Pick the rule your destination states, enter your dates, and check.</p><div class='calc' id='pv'><div class='cmp'><label>Passport expiry date<input type='date' id='pe'></label><label>Passport issue date <span class='mute'>(Schengen check)</span><input type='date' id='pi'></label><label>Entry date<input type='date' id='pen'></label><label>Exit date<input type='date' id='pex'></label><label>Rule to check<select id='pr'><option value='stay'>Valid for the whole stay</option><option value='in3'>3 months after entry</option><option value='in6'>6 months after entry</option><option value='out3'>3 months after departure</option><option value='out6'>6 months after departure</option><option value='sch'>Schengen: 3 months after departure, issued within 10 years</option></select></label></div><div id='pres' class='result' aria-live='polite'></div></div><h2>The common rules</h2><ul><li><strong>Six-month rule:</strong> some countries want at least six months of validity, counted from your arrival or your departure. The destination decides which.</li><li><strong>Three-month rule:</strong> the Schengen Area requires validity of at least three months after you plan to leave, and the passport must have been issued within the previous 10 years.</li><li><strong>Length of stay:</strong> some countries only need the passport to be valid for the whole stay.</li><li><strong>Blank pages:</strong> some countries also require one or two blank pages.</li></ul><p class='note'>Rules differ by country and change. We do not publish a country-by-country list because we could not verify one from an authoritative source. Find your destination's rule on its official site (linked on each destination page), then pick it above.</p><noscript><p>Turn on JavaScript to use the checker.</p></noscript>")
